Maintainer: Çağan ERGÜN <73942784+caganerg@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/caganerg/samsung-ml2160-rust
Description: CUPS raster filter for Samsung ML-2160 series printers
 rastertospl-rust converts the CUPS raster stream (RaSt/RaS2/RaS3) into the
 native SPL2 / QPDL v3 format spoken by Samsung ML-2160, ML-2165, ML-2165W
 and ML-2168 monochrome laser printers: PJL job envelope, 17-byte page
 header, Algo 0x11 RLE-compressed band records and checksums.
 .
 The package ships the filter binary and the matching PPD.
 .
 This control file still describes the 1.x filter; the 2.0 Printer Application
 packaging lands with the migration. Two of its dependency lines are already
 correct for 2.0 and are recorded now because nothing derives them
 automatically:
 .
 libcups2-dev / libcups2t64 are named explicitly because of risk R-6. PAPPL
 embeds the CUPS raster page header by value in its print-options structure,
 so libcups defines part of the ABI we compile against — but the binary
 references no libcups symbol, so the linker drops -lcups and
 ${shlibs:Depends} records nothing for it. The dependency is real and has to
 be stated by hand.
 .
 libpappl-dev is bounded to the >= 1.3, < 2.0 range that build.rs enforces
 (decision Q-1); the runtime side comes from ${shlibs:Depends} via the
 library's symbols file.
